  "question": {
    "text": "Figure shows three resistor configurations $R_1, R_2$ and $R_3$ connected to $3 \\mathrm{~V}$ battery. If the power dissipated by the configuration $R_1, R_2$ and $R_3$ is $P_1, P_2$ and $P_3$, respectively, then\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/FaDLcWdj6MIA-JqWZmTiJ6nR8EgzVH5Cszu_B_UC_vs.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "iCQen",
      "text": "\n$P_1>P_2>P_3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nODNy",
      "text": "\n$P_1>P_3>P_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gyP6D",
      "text": "\n$P_2>P_1>P_3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Ha8Tm",
      "text": "\n$P_3>P_2>P_1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Applying $P=\\frac{V^2}{R}$\n$R_1=1 \\Omega, R_2=0.5 \\Omega$ and $R_3=2 \\Omega, V_1=V_2=V_3=3$ volt\n$\\therefore \\quad P_1=\\frac{(3)^2}{1}=9 \\mathrm{~W}$\n$\\quad P_2=\\frac{(3)^2}{0.5}=18 \\mathrm{~W}$ and $P_3=\\frac{(3)^2}{2}=4.5 \\mathrm{~W}$\n$\\therefore \\quad P_2>P_1>P_3$\n$\\therefore \\quad$ correct option is (c).",
    "image": null
  },
